 ### Metrics
 
+The KVMem integration adds `kvmem.cache_reuse` to generation responses and the
+same fields to the unified request monitor: `planned_cached_tokens`,
+`actual_cached_tokens`, `planned_cache_source` and `cache_source` (`own`,
+`shared`, `miss`). The existing cached-token wire accounting remains the exact
+admission quote. A best-effort failed restore can recompute that quoted prefix;
+the independent native actual observation is zero in that case. An unobserved
+value is null, including runtime families without this observation. This does
+not change the native timing or Prometheus series' existing meaning.
+
+KVMem memory summaries distinguish logical owner bytes from the global native
+physical H/D charge, sealed-record references from unique allocations, and
+logical/physical read-only checkpoint bytes. Shared records are charged once;
+selectors, MeanK, graph feedback, Query state and mutable GPU state remain
+private. These counters do not bound process RSS or represent VRAM savings.
+
 `GET /metrics` serves the Prometheus text format, also on `--stats-port`. Like `/v1/load` it
 requires the API key when one is configured and reads only already-published counters. The
